Guix build sandbox workaround: force ghostty's SIMD code path off so the
libghostty-vt target stays compatible with the baseline CPU used by zig
build.  In 0.48.0 ghostel gates SIMD via the ghostty_simd build option
(true on non-Termux); pin the local binding to false rather than touching
the ghostty dependency block.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Guix-specific build environment]

--- a/build.zig
+++ b/build.zig
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 
     // On-device Termux builds have no NDK, whose sysroot ghostty's vendored
     // simdutf/highway C++ builds require; use ghostty's scalar path there.
-    const ghostty_simd = if (android_libc) |libc| libc.source != .termux else true;
+    const ghostty_simd = false;
     const ghostty_dep = b.dependency("ghostty", .{
         .target = target,
         .optimize = ghostty_optimize,
